{"term":"respective","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:f713458b34f4d7f264","definition":"Relating to particular persons or things, each to each; particular; own.","example":"They returned to their respective places of abode.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["corresponding","relevant","specific"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["corespective","disrespective","irrespective","respectively","respectiveness","unrespective"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/respective#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:95241d3f7a83a1dd4b","definition":"Noticing with attention; careful; wary.","example":"c. 1559-1570, Edwin Sandys, letter to Bernard Gilpin\nBut if you looke upon the estate of the church of England with a respective eye , you cannot with a good conscience refuse this charge imposed upon you","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable, obsolete","register":"not-comparable, obsolete","wordFamily":["corespective","disrespective","irrespective","respectively","respectiveness","unrespective"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/respective#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:616ea5c951a4e4001e","definition":"Looking toward; having reference to; relative, not absolute.","example":"the respective connections of society","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable, obsolete","register":"not-comparable, obsolete","wordFamily":["corespective","disrespective","irrespective","respectively","respectiveness","unrespective"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/respective#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:376d99b9035f2160de",